  "content": {
    "id": "p17-p1-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "1",
    "prompt": "Let $g(x)$ be an even function and $f(x)$ be any function. Define the composition $$h(x)=f(g(x)).$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p17-p1-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that $h(-x)=f(g(x))$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$h(-x)=f(g(-x))=f(g(x))$, since $g$ is even.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}h(-x)&=f(g(-x))\\\\h(-x)&=f(g(x)).\\end{align*}$$ The second equality uses $g(-x)=g(x)$, since $g$ is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 17
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-p1-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What can we say about the function $h(x)$?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$h$ is an even function.",
          "worked": "Since $h(-x)=f(g(x))=h(x)$, $h$ is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p17-p1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Hence, what can we say about the composition of two functions if the ‘inside’ function is even?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The composition is even.",
          "worked": "An even inside function gives equal outputs at $x$ and $-x$. Applying the outside function therefore gives $h(-x)=h(x)$, so the composition is even.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      }
    ]
  },
